{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791064454,"nonce":"eVu3gOiF7gqGaYu90M67QNzg0iQ=","title":"Built-in HTML elements: form controls, text and structure, a user-agent stylesheet, a top layer","message":"ashui's built-ins are HTML's built-in elements, as lowercase hxx tags that need no import, behaving as HTML specifies. A cn-like component library (shadcn-style) is a separate standalone ashui.components library, later; it is not this. Blinc's blinc_layout/src/widgets is a reference for behaviour only.\n\nDecided (user, 2026-10-03):\n- Tags and attributes are HTML's.\n- State: HTML's attribute names; a signal makes it two-way, a constant sets it once (checked={agreed}, \u003cselect value={fruit}\u003e). Radios share a signal through group=, as Svelte's bind:group does.\n- Default looks come from a user-agent stylesheet in CSS: type selectors themed with var() tokens, so authors restyle with CSS or Tw.\n\nElements:\n- form controls: button; input of type checkbox, radio, range, number, text, password, search, email; select with option and optgroup; textarea; label; fieldset and legend; output\n- interactive: a, details/summary, dialog, progress, meter\n- text and structure: hr, h1-h6, p, span, strong, em, small, code, pre, blockquote, ul/ol/li\n\nBehaviour per HTML: Space and Enter on buttons and checkboxes; arrows move among radios of a name; a label operates its control; select opens a list (arrows, typeahead, Escape); a modal dialog keeps focus and closes on Escape; a disabled fieldset disables what it holds. CSS gains :checked, :indeterminate and :placeholder-shown.\n\nNeeds a top layer, as HTML's: select's list and a modal dialog draw above everything, placed against their trigger, dismissed by an outside click or Escape.\n\nStages:\n1. Import-free tags; the text elements; the user-agent stylesheet loaded under authors' sheets.\n2. button, checkbox and radio (group=), label, :checked.\n3. The top layer; select/option/optgroup; dialog; details/summary.\n4. range, number and the text inputs over TextField; progress, meter, output; fieldset/legend; a.\n5. Lists, tables, pre/code/blockquote.","files":null}]}